14: def main(input_grid):
15:     """
16:     Fit two monochromatic puzzle pieces together into the tightest rectangular assembly.
17: 
18:     Input structure:
19:     - The input is a black grid containing exactly two non-black monochromatic objects.
20:     - Each object is a puzzle piece that may be translated but not rotated.
21:     - The pieces come from a compact two-color object.
22: 
23:     Rule:
24:     - Crop the two pieces from the input.
25:     - Try all non-overlapping translations on a canvas large enough to hold both pieces.
26:     - Return the placement whose cropped bounding box leaves the fewest black cells.
27: 
28:     Key insight:
29:     - The reconstruction is the densest translation-only packing of the two pieces.
30:     """
31:     # Plan:
32:     # 1. Detect the pieces
33:     # 2. Consider different ways of placing them together
34:     # 3. Pick the way which makes them the most tightly packed, meaning that there is as little empty pixels remaining as possible
